; Stage 15 W3b: the §1.5 accept criterion — `(import-use "SDL2/SDL.h")` no longer
; produces invalid IR. SDL.h is the umbrella-header stress test: it transitively
; reaches the x86 intrinsics headers, whose `void _mm_clflush(void const *__p)`
; used to import as `declare void @_mm_clflush(void, ptr)` and kill the whole
; compilation at `failed to parse generated IR`.
;
; run_w3b_sdl builds this with `-o` (a real link), NOT `--emit-llvm`: --emit-llvm
; never parses the IR it writes, so exit 0 there is not evidence of a valid
; module. Nothing here CALLS an SDL function, so no -lSDL2 is needed — the
; declarations alone are what is under test.
(import-use "SDL2/SDL.h")

; The spec's own two-line probe (cheader.md "Verified repro"): an opaque handle
; type in a `defn` signature.
(defn f (w:ptr:SDL_Window):i32 (return 0))

(defn main ():i32
  (printf "w3b-sdl ok\n")
  (return 0))
